# Database Patterns and Best Practices

## Database Configuration
- Use environment variables for database configuration
- Configuration is loaded through [Brain/ct_brain.php](mdc:Brain/ct_brain.php)
- Database settings are defined in `.env` file

## Core Database Classes
- [Brain/Classes/database/Database.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/database/Database.php) - Main database connection
- [Brain/Classes/database/DBORM.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/database/DBORM.php) - Object-Relational Mapping
- [Brain/Classes/database/Transaction.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/database/Transaction.php) - Transaction management
- [Brain/Classes/database/DBMigration.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/database/DBMigration.php) - Database migrations

## Model Patterns

### Basic Model Structure
```php
class UserModel extends Model
{
    protected $table = 'users';
    protected $primaryKey = 'id';
    protected $fillable = ['name', 'email', 'password'];
    
    // Define relationships
    public function posts()
    {
        return $this->hasMany(PostModel::class);
    }
}
```

### Database Operations
- Always use prepared statements
- Use transactions for multi-step operations
- Implement proper error handling
- Use the ORM for complex queries when appropriate

### Query Patterns
```php
// Using Database class directly
$db = $registry->get('database');
$users = $db->query("SELECT * FROM users WHERE status = ?", ['active']);

// Using Model ORM
$users = UserModel::where('status', 'active')->get();
```

## Migration Patterns
- Use [Brain/Classes/database/DBMigration.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/database/DBMigration.php)
- Create migration files for schema changes
- Include both up and down methods
- Test migrations in development environment

## Caching Patterns
- Use [Brain/Classes/database/CacheStore.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/database/CacheStore.php)
- Cache frequently accessed data
- Implement cache invalidation strategies
- Use appropriate cache TTL values

## Security Considerations
- Always validate input data
- Use parameterized queries
- Implement proper access controls
- Log database operations for auditing
- Use connection pooling for performance

## Performance Optimization
- Use indexes appropriately
- Optimize query performance
- Implement query result caching
- Use database connection pooling
- Monitor slow queries